## Unsupported-browser story

`isPasskeySupported()` checks both `window.isSecureContext` and
`window.PublicKeyCredential`. This is deliberately stricter than a bare
`Boolean(window.PublicKeyCredential)` check: without the secure-context test, a
misconfigured dev origin (see below) fails with a raw `TypeError` instead of a
clean, handled "not supported" branch.

Gate your two surfaces on it differently:

- **Login screen** - don't render the passkey button at all when unsupported.
  There is nothing useful to say to someone who cannot use the feature on a
  screen that already offers password (and optionally Google SSO).
- **Passkey management screen** - render an explicit message instead of a
  disabled control, so a user who came looking for passkey settings learns why
  they are absent.

## Secure context and RP ID

WebAuthn only runs in a secure context:

| Dev URL | Works? | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `http://localhost:5173` | Yes | `localhost` is a trustworthy origin by spec, even over plain HTTP |
| `http://127.0.0.1:5173` | Yes | Same rule |
| `https://myapp.test` (mkcert/Valet TLS) | Yes | Secure context |
| `http://myapp.test` (Valet/Herd default HTTP) | No | Not `localhost`, not HTTPS - `window.isSecureContext` is `false` |
| `http://192.168.1.20:5173` (LAN, phone testing) | No | Same as above - this is the one that bites, because testing a platform authenticator on a phone is exactly when you reach for a LAN IP |

Fix: terminate TLS locally (`mkcert`, or Herd/Valet's `secure` command) and set
`PASSKEY_RP_ID` accordingly.

**The RP-ID rule.** `PASSKEY_RP_ID` must be the origin's own host or a
registrable parent domain of it - never a sibling. If your frontend and API
live on different subdomains (`app.example.com` and `api.example.com`),
`PASSKEY_RP_ID` must be the shared parent (`example.com`). Getting this wrong
surfaces as a browser `SecurityError` with **no authenticator prompt at all** -
indistinguishable, from the user's side, from nothing happening.
`mapPasskeyCeremonyError()` surfaces `DOMException.name` verbatim for exactly
this reason: don't hide it behind a generic message.

## Interaction with two-factor authentication

If you've also generated the `two-factor-authentication` feature: a passkey
login returns a real `token_type: "Bearer"` and therefore **bypasses the
generated 2FA challenge pipeline**, which only runs inside the password login
flow. This is deliberate - the passkey stands in for the two-factor code
rather than adding to it - and is not something this package patches for you.
If you want both factors stacked instead, that is a change to your backend's
`LoginAction` pipe list, not to anything generated here.

## API contract

| Function | Path | Auth | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `getPasskeyRegistrationOptions` | `{{ passkeyRegistrationOptionsEndpoint }}` | Bearer token | Feed the result straight into `createPasskeyCredential()` - its casing is the browser's own, never camelCased |
| `createPasskey` | `{{ passkeysEndpoint }}` (POST) | Bearer token | Completes enrollment; returns the new `Passkey` |
| `listPasskeys` | `{{ passkeysEndpoint }}` (GET) | Bearer token | Backs `usePasskeys` |
| `deletePasskey` | `{{ passkeysEndpoint }}/{id}` (DELETE) | Bearer token | Returns no content |
| `getPasskeyLoginOptions` | `{{ passkeyLoginOptionsEndpoint }}` | None | Public - this is how an unauthenticated visitor starts a passkey login |
| `loginWithPasskey` | `{{ passkeyLoginEndpoint }}` | None | Echoes back the `ceremonyId` from the options call |

## Screens to build

- **Passkey login button** - calls `useSignInWithPasskey()`, gated by
  `isPasskeySupported()`.
- **Passkey management list** - calls `usePasskeys({ token })` and
  `useDeletePasskey()`; gate on `isPasskeySupported()` per the message above,
  not by hiding the whole screen.
- **Passkey enrollment** - a name prompt (validated with `getPasskeyNameSchema()`)
  followed by `useEnrolPasskey()`.

None of these have a reference screen to port from an existing app - design
them to fit your own account-settings and login patterns.

